    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 394,
        "y": 3915,
        "w": 651,
        "h": 60
      },
      "type": "heading",
      "tag": "h3",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Arenas and encounters",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "45px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "center",
        "lineHeight": "60.3px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 309,
        "y": 4047,
        "w": 820,
        "h": 105
      },
      "type": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "level": null,
      "text": "During the development of Bugs N’ Guns, I was in charge of designing all the combat and encounters in the game.\nIn this section, I will explain the process of designing two of the game’s arenas.",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "20px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "start",
        "lineHeight": "35px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 4323,
        "w": 407,
        "h": 60
      },
      "type": "heading",
      "tag": "h3",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "First Game Arena",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "45px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "center",
        "lineHeight": "60.3px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": -88,
        "y": 4383,
        "w": 613,
        "h": 652
      },
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1f3734_d3c56467562b4c34ac5d923c9e292d8a~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_613,h_652,al_c,lg_1,q_90,enc_avif,quality_auto/1f3734_d3c56467562b4c34ac5d923c9e292d8a~mv2.png",
      "srcset": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1f3734_d3c56467562b4c34ac5d923c9e292d8a~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_613,h_652,al_c,lg_1,q_90,enc_avif,quality_auto/1f3734_d3c56467562b4c34ac5d923c9e292d8a~mv2.png 1x, https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1f3734_d3c56467562b4c34ac5d923c9e292d8a~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_677,h_720,al_c,lg_1,q_90,enc_avif,quality_auto/1f3734_d3c56467562b4c34ac5d923c9e292d8a~mv2.png 2x",
      "alt": "image.png",
      "name": null,
      "original": null,
      "natural": {
        "w": 613,
        "h": 652
      },
      "background": false,
      "link": null,
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 4426,
        "w": 820,
        "h": 140
      },
      "type": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "level": null,
      "text": "This is the first arena in the game, so it needed to introduce the basic mechanics and dynamics of gameplay (combining weapons) in a controlled and accessible environment for players.",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "20px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "start",
        "lineHeight": "35px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 4566,
        "w": 820,
        "h": 140
      },
      "type": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "level": null,
      "text": "The train runs alongside a pit from which no enemies can emerge, ensuring that players only need to focus on one side of the train. This reduces the arena’s intensity, allowing players to concentrate on learning the mechanics without worrying about defending the train from multiple directions.",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "20px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "start",
        "lineHeight": "35px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 4741,
        "w": 820,
        "h": 175
      },
      "type": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "level": null,
      "text": "Naturally, the enemies in this arena are the most basic Smashers in the game. Their sole purpose is to serve as practice targets for players, posing a low, though not nonexistent, threat. Because of how these enemies function, arriving in waves, players must learn to combine their weapons to defeat them, which is the core gunplay mechanic.",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "20px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "start",
        "lineHeight": "35px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 4951,
        "w": 820,
        "h": 140
      },
      "type": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "level": null,
      "text": "At the end of the arena, the final enemy spawn will appear climbing down one of the rock walls in the environment. This is intended to teach players that enemies can climb and bypass obstacles, and that players can use their weapons to “paint” the walls the enemies traverse and defeat them before they reach the ground.",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "20px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "start",
        "lineHeight": "35px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 5372,
        "w": 451,
        "h": 60
      },
      "type": "heading",
      "tag": "h3",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Fourth Game Arena",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "45px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "center",
        "lineHeight": "60.3px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": -76,
        "y": 5432,
        "w": 613,
        "h": 660
      },
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1f3734_ac732184f3ad4e2ab3998265c3c383d4~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_613,h_660,al_c,lg_1,q_90,enc_avif,quality_auto/1f3734_ac732184f3ad4e2ab3998265c3c383d4~mv2.png",
      "srcset": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1f3734_ac732184f3ad4e2ab3998265c3c383d4~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_613,h_660,al_c,lg_1,q_90,enc_avif,quality_auto/1f3734_ac732184f3ad4e2ab3998265c3c383d4~mv2.png 1x, https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1f3734_ac732184f3ad4e2ab3998265c3c383d4~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_668,h_720,al_c,lg_1,q_90,enc_avif,quality_auto/1f3734_ac732184f3ad4e2ab3998265c3c383d4~mv2.png 2x",
      "alt": "image.png",
      "name": null,
      "original": null,
      "natural": {
        "w": 613,
        "h": 660
      },
      "background": false,
      "link": null,
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 5464,
        "w": 820,
        "h": 105
      },
      "type": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "level": null,
      "text": "This arena is placed right after players receive their second weapon kit, the Electroplasma and the Hydrogel.",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "20px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "start",
        "lineHeight": "35px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 5569,
        "w": 820,
        "h": 175
      },
      "type": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "level": null,
      "text": "In this arena, the train will remain stationary at one end, while enemies attack in waves. The pacing and intensity of these waves are controlled through the enemy counter and the AI Director, allowing the encounter to maintain a controlled difficulty level.",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
        "font": "prompt, sans-serif",
        "size": "20px",
        "weight": "400",
        "color": "rgb(255, 255, 255)",
        "align": "start",
        "lineHeight": "35px",
        "letterSpacing": "normal",
        "transform": "none",
        "italic": false
      }
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "rect": {
        "x": 752,
        "y": 5744,
        "w": 820,
        "h": 175
      },
      "type": "text",
      "tag": "p",
      "level": null,
      "text": "The main goal of this arena is to allow players to experiment and have fun with their newly acquired weapons. Because of this, the overall challenge is intentionally kept at a moderate level, prioritizing learning and player expression over high pressure.",
      "links": [],
      "style": {
